The consideration of DigiGraff’s social acceptability is important, as if users are unwilling to use projection in public, any benefits brought by its deep embedding of data into the environment will be lost.
Group participation outdoors made projection feel like a collaborative “project,” increasing confidence and reducing self-consciousness.
Offering both projector and non-projector versions allowed users to switch based on social comfort and context.
Having found that using DigiGraff without projection was socially comfortable in nearly all contexts. To solve this, we can add a “preview” mode on the phone screen so users know the position, and content before projecting, reducing anxiety about showing something unintended.
